{"With FGAP v2 enabled the registerListener callback never fires because the guard only checks ADMIN_FINE_GRAINED_AUTHZ, causing realms that rely solely on ADMIN_FINE_GRAINED_AUTHZ_V2 to leak permissions for deleted roles/clients/groups since no listener resets them": 0.8901398777961731, "getClientsWithPermission adds the schema-wide 'Clients' resource to the returned set when a realm-level policy exists, but callers expect actual client IDs and will fail to resolve a client with ID 'Clients'": 0.7164384126663208, "canMapRoles() with V2 FGAP enabled removes the fallback that allowed administrators holding manage-clients or canManage(client) capability to map roles, causing existing admins to get 403 on role-mapping operations until custom permissions are created": 0.8536906242370605, "canMapCompositeRoles and canMapClientScopeRoles have the same missing fallback issue as canMapRoles, breaking those admin flows when FGAP v2 is enabled": 0.8651762008666992}